[17.985, "\u001b[H\u001b[5GPIECE output matches every piece in th\u001b[44G fixtures, including \u001b[67Gw-byte tokens.\u001b[82G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GFIXED argmaxes ma\u001b[23Gch\u001b[27Ghe\u001b[30Gfixture tokens.\u001b[46G\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BThe edge cases\u001b[20Gwork: an emp\u001b[33Gy prompt, \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mGENERATE 0\u001b[39m, \u001b[56Gtopping o\u001b[66G token 1, and QUIT\u001b[85Gexiting\u001b[93Gwith code\u00a00.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GA 691-token p\u001b[19Gompt produced\u001b[33Gexactly\u001b[41G334\u001b[45Gnew\u001b[49Gtokens\u001b[56Gbefore\u001b[63Greporting\u001b[73G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mcontext\u001b[39m.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mChanges that don't change the numbers\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BAt load,\u001b[14Gthe weights\u001b[26Gare copied into an al\u001b[48Ggned buffer instead of read in pl\u001b[82Gce from\u001b[90Gthe\u001b[94Gfile.\u001b[100GThey\u001b[105Gare\u001b[109Gthe\u001b[113Gsame\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bfloat32\u001b[13Gvalues,\u001b[21Gand\u001b[25Git\u001b[28Gmeasured\u001b[37Gabout\u001b[43G10%\u001b[47Gfaster.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[6Ghe RoPE \u001b[16Gs/\u001b[19Gin val\u001b[26Ges are comput\u001b[40Gd once per token instead of once per\u001b[77Glayer. Th\u001b[87Gy don't\u001b[95Gdepend\u001b[102Gon\u001b[105Gthe\u001b[109Glayer,\u001b[116Gso\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bthe\u001b[9Gvalues\u001b[16Gare\u001b[20Gidentical.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K"]
[17.987, "\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mLimitations\r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m  - Results are not bit-exact with the reference, because Accelerate adds up the products in a different order. A\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B    near-tie between two top tokens could in principle pick a different token on other inputs.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  - Accelerate may use several threads internally unless the harness limits it. The program leaves that to the harness,\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bas\u001b[8Gthe\u001b[12Grules\u001b[18Grequire.\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G- For inputs the interface do\u001b[33Gsn't define, I made choices: FIXED/LOGITS with\u001b[80Gmore\u001b[85Gthan\u001b[90G1024\u001b[95Gids\u001b[99Gprocess\u001b[107Gonly\u001b[112Gthe\u001b[116Gfirst\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B1024,\u001b[11Gand\u001b[15Gbad\u001b[19Gids\u001b[23Gor\u001b[26Gan\u001b[29Gunwritable\u001b[40GLOGITS\u001b[47Gpath\u001b[52Ganswer\u001b[59G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mERR ...\u001b[39m.\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G- Speed\u001b[11Gis about 65\u201372 tokens/s on\u001b[38Gthis machine\u001b[51Gwith\u001b[56GAccelerate's\u001b[69Gdefault\u001b[77Gthreading.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BNOTES.md records the build command, every command I ran, and these points\u001b[77Gin\u001b[80Gmore\u001b[85Gdetail.\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u273b\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mCrunched for "]
[17.988, "4m 51s \u00b7 done 4:20 PM\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;240;240;240m\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u276f \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mProfile this implementation on the supplied development workloads. Improve performance within the same rules and \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mremaining budget. Preserve the interface and correctness requirements. Do not use hidden evaluation inputs, external \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mimplementations or other ports. Record profiling evidence, changes, tests and remaining limitations in NOTES.md.\u001b[39m      \r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m I'll start by finding the development wo\u001b[44Gkloads\u001b[51Gand measuring a baseline.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u23fa\u001b[39m L\u001b[6Gting files and checking machine\u001b[38Gdetails\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  \u23bf  $ ls -la; /usr/sbin/sysctl -n machdep.cpu.brand_string hw.ncpu hw.perflevel0.physicalcpu hw.memsize \r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[5G \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mhw.perflevel0.l2cachesize 2>&1; env | grep -iE 'veclib|omp|thread'\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m\u2736\u001b[3GTwisting\u2026 \u001b[3"]
